# Playing

## Starting a game

Pick a game and press **A**. The game slides into its console and starts. The first time you play a console, a card shows
which button is which; press **A** to go on.

If a game cannot start, you are back on the shelf at once and a note says why; **A** or **B** closes it. That includes a
game for another emulator app that Android couldn't open.

**3DS games in Azahar:** open Azahar once and finish its first-start setup before you start a 3DS game from pocket-ui.
Before that setup Azahar closes right away; when a game comes back that soon, the note says so.

## The pause menu

Press **HOME** in a game, or Android's **Back**. The menu looks and works as on the handhelds: the rows under each
other at the left, the save's picture at the right.

- **Continue**: back to the game (**B** or **Back** too).
- **Save** and **Load**: eight save slots for each game. Left and Right choose the slot; the picture shows what is in it.
- **Earlier**: goes back if something went wrong. A moment is kept when the game starts and every 5 minutes of play,
  with its picture when the emulator has supplied one. Left and Right choose how far back, and the row says how long ago it was.
- **Options**: **Zoom** (the picture larger, to read small text), **Screenshot**, then the picture (scaling, look,
  screen frame), sound and the emulator's own settings.
- **Achievements**: when you are signed in to RetroAchievements.
- **Save & quit**: keeps the moment and goes back to the shelf.

## Low battery

At 5% on battery a line over the game says so. At 2% the game is saved and you are back on the shelf: charge the
handheld, and **A** on the game goes on from that moment. On the charger nothing happens, however low.

## Continue

Your last game stands first on the shelf. **A** on it goes straight back to the moment you left. Save & quit keeps that
moment, and so does leaving the game any other way: Android's launcher, another app, or the power button. Come back
through the app and the game waits in its pause menu.

## Sleep

Press the power button in a game: the screen goes off and pocket-ui keeps the moment. Press it again and the game goes
on where you were, as on pocket-ui OS; a pause menu you had open stays open. Without a PIN, pattern or password on your
lock screen, the game comes back straight away; with one, Android asks for it first.

## Which systems play where

- **In pocket-ui's own player:** Game Boy, Game Boy Color, Game Boy Advance, NES, SNES, Master System, Game Gear, Mega Drive,
  PC Engine, WonderSwan, Atari 2600, Atari Lynx, Neo Geo Pocket, PlayStation, Nintendo DS, Nintendo 64, PSP, Saturn and
  Dreamcast, all in the app, nothing to download. Saturn needs a BIOS from your own console in `ROMs/bios`. An emulator app
  you have installed that plays a system can be chosen on the game's **Runs on** page instead.
- **Still being tested:** Nintendo 64, PSP, Saturn and Dreamcast in pocket-ui's own player. Not every game runs at full
  speed yet, and the sound can stutter in places; keep an extra save in the game itself for these four.
- **PlayStation 2, GameCube, Wii, 3DS and Xbox** play in an emulator app you have installed. pocket-ui starts the game in it
  and you come back to the shelf when you leave it.

No games or BIOS files come with pocket-ui.
